cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "qec-engine"
abstract: >-
  AdaptiveRG-QEC is a research prototype of a Monte-Carlo and
  Monte-Carlo-renormalization-group (MCRG) verification harness for
  quantum-error-correction thresholds. It combines an adaptive Metropolis
  kernel with a Foster-Lyapunov drift guard, MCRG estimators for critical
  exponents of the Ising model, a random-bond Ising model on the Nishimori
  line, QEC code diagnostics (repetition code; rotated surface code with
  MWPM decoding via Stim and PyMatching as an optional extra) and
  convergence diagnostics (autocorrelation-aware errors, CLT variance,
  rank-normalized R-hat, exact total-variation mixing). Some gates compare
  against an independent closed-form or exact oracle; others are
  consistency checks, directional controls or empirical comparisons. The
  Phase-5 run and the QEC manifest-v2 path replay bit-identically from a run
  manifest. It is not a frontier threshold tool.
authors:
  - name: "Coworker Research (Coworkerz)"
# Development version of the current tree (adaptiverg_qec.__version__); the
# last tagged release is v0.4.0 (2026-06-19) and predates e.g. Phase 7.
version: "0.5.0.dev0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcohost33-maker/qec-engine"
keywords:
  - quantum-error-correction
  - monte-carlo
  - mcmc
  - renormalization-group
  - ising-model
  - nishimori-line
  - surface-code
  - reproducibility
